<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Take the "Picked" tick box off the transfer lines.

        WHY
        ===
        Odoo decides what to ship from the per-line ``picked`` flag, and the
        rule in stock/models/stock_picking.py::_pre_action_done_hook is:

            if has_quantity and not has_pick:
                picking.move_ids.picked = True

        So if NOTHING is ticked, Odoo helpfully marks the whole transfer
        picked and ships it in full. But the moment ONE line is ticked,
        has_pick is True, that blanket assignment is skipped, and
        _action_done then drops every line that was left unticked:

            moves_todo = moves.filtered(lambda m: not (m.state == 'cancel'
                or (m.quantity <= 0 and not m.is_inventory) or not m.picked))

        Those lines process as zero and are cancelled or pushed to a
        backorder, even though the stock was on hand and reserved. To the
        person clicking Validate the quantity simply changed by itself.

        UFS hit this for real. UFS/PICK/00064 completed with a line for 5
        showing done 0 and picked false, and at the time of writing 160 open
        move lines are reserved but unticked, every one of them exposed to
        the same thing the moment a single sibling line gets ticked. The
        knock-on effect is stock drift: goods leave the building, Odoo never
        records it, and a fresh physical count is wrong within days.

        WHAT THIS DOES
        ==============
        Odoo already ships this column as ``optional="hide"``, so it is off
        by default and was switched on here at some point. Turning it back
        off through the column picker only helps the user who does it,
        because that choice is stored per user. Forcing column_invisible
        removes it for everyone regardless of their saved preference, which
        is what "team-wide" requires.

        With no tick box on screen, nothing gets half-ticked, so the safe
        branch above always applies and transfers ship in full. Partial
        deliveries still work the normal way: edit the Quantity on the line
        and let Odoo raise the backorder.

        SCOPE
        =====
        This only touches the Operations list on the transfer form. It does
        not change the field, so the barcode app and any automation that
        legitimately sets ``picked`` are unaffected, and nothing in the
        server-side validation logic changes.
    -->
    <record id="view_picking_form_ufs_hide_picked" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">stock.picking.form.ufs.hide.picked</field>
        <field name="model">stock.picking</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="stock.view_picking_form"/>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <!--
                Anchored through move_ids/list so it cannot accidentally
                match a "picked" field in another embedded list.
            -->
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='move_ids']/list/field[@name='picked']"
                   position="attributes">
                <attribute name="column_invisible">1</attribute>
                <attribute name="optional">hide</attribute>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
